{#- The account's own menu, opened from its initials. It imposes nothing but
    its frame: who is signed in at its head — and, when the application says
    it, as what (`role_labels`, one line each; `role_label` for a single one)
    —, and leaving at its foot. Every entry between is the application's: its
    own (`items`), then its closing ones (`items_end`: terms, policies). The
    pages this package offers — `user_profile_index`, `user_totp_index`, and
    `account_administration_url()` for an account allowed to administer — are
    for the application to list there or not.
    What only development has — switching account, the mailbox — is in the
    footer's development menu (DevMenuProviderInterface), not here.
    Drawn by the design system's button_menu. -#}
{%- set user = app.user -%}
{%- set roles = role_labels|default(role_label|default(null) ? [role_label] : []) -%}
{%- set entries = [{ heading: user.displayName, lines: roles }]|merge(items|default([])) -%}
{%- if items_end|default([]) is not empty -%}
    {%- set entries = entries|merge([{ separator: true }])|merge(items_end) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set entries = entries|merge([
    { separator: true },
    { icon: 'ph:bold/sign-out', label: 'WexampleSymfonyUserDsBundle.common.menu::logout' | trans, href: path('user_security_logout') },
]) -%}
{{ button_menu(null, null, entries, {
    class: 'button--flat',
    avatar: user.initials,
    menu_align: 'right',
    attr: { 'aria-label': 'WexampleSymfonyUserDsBundle.common.menu::label' | trans, title: user.displayName },
}) }}
